\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Void Profiles}: Sharp edges from $\Phi$ peaks, testable via Euclid lensing (2024).
\item \textbf{Redshift}: $z \approx \exp\left[\frac{\chi}{2} \int_\gamma \partial_s \Phi , ds\right]$, deviating from $\Lambda$CDM at $z &gt; 2.5$ (DESI).
\item \textbf{CMB Anomalies}: Axis of Evil and cold spot as $\Phi$-$S$ correlations.
\item \textbf{Halo Profiles}: Modified by $\Phi$-driven repulsion, affecting cluster mass functions.
\item \textbf{MOND-like Effects}: $\Phi$ gradients mimic low-acceleration dynamics.
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Discussion}
RSVP eliminates the need for dark energy, inflation, and dark matter by modeling the universe as a computationally ergodic plenum. Its falsifiability lies in distinct void lensing, high-$z$ BAO shifts, and CMB signatures. Future work includes GPU-accelerated 512$^3$ simulations and coupling to Boltzmann codes for CMB predictions.</p>
