\subsection{Type Ia Supernovae}
The redshift $1+z \approx \exp(\chi \int \partial_s S ds / 2)$ fits luminosity distance $d_L = (1+z) \int dz / H(z)$, matching ZTF SN Ia DR2 (2025) with $\chi \sim 10^{-3}$ Mpc$^{-1}$, resolving Hubble tension via $S$ anisotropy.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection{CMB Angular Power Spectrum}
Entropy-driven oscillations produce acoustic peaks at $\ell \sim 220$, comparable to $\Lambda$CDM, without expansion, via torsion-phase correlations.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection{BAO and Galaxy Surveys}
$S$-integrated paths match DESI BAO at $z \sim 0.11$, with 5% shifts at $z &gt; 2.5$.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Predictions and Tests}
\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Void Lensing}: Sharper shear profiles from $\Phi$ peaks (Euclid, 2024+).
\item \textbf{BAO}: 5% peak shifts at $z &gt; 2.5$ (DESI).
\item \textbf{CMB}: Enhanced low-multipole power; cold spot as $\Phi$-min/$S$-max well (Planck/JWST).
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Falsifiability and Risk Assessment}
RSVP is falsifiable if:</p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">SN Ia $z &gt; 2$ curves deviate from \eqref{eq:redshift}.</li>
<li class="break-words">CMB lensing lacks predicted torsion-induced peaks.</li>
