<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">$\Lambda$CDM outperforms in BBN precision; RSVP requires tighter $\Phi$ constraints. Risks: Observational confirmation of $\Lambda$CDMâ€™s expansion (e.g., via new CMB data) could challenge RSVP, mitigated by focusing on anomaly resolution.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Discussion and Outlook}
RSVP extends thermodynamic cosmology, aligning with modern nonequilibrium frameworks. Unique predictions include torsion-driven spin alignments and entropy-gradient Hubble variance. Future work: GPU simulations ($512^3$), Boltzmann code integration, and survey tests.</p>
