</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(1188px);"><span><span>The historical context of cosmology reveals a progression from static models to expanding ones, driven by Hubble's law and CMB discovery. However, anomalies suggest revisiting static paradigms with thermodynamic twists. RSVP integrates insights from Bianconi's entropy-derived gravity </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{Bianconi2025}, Carroll and Remmen's distinction between holographic and thermodynamic gravity </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{CarrollRemmen2016}, and Darmos's space particle dualism </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{Darmos2021}, where gravity arises from baryon counts rather than mass-energy.
</span></span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(1209.6px);"><span>
